{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"9e048dec607a78227c18b4e4a5cd3ac589191060bd8788e31d28be68fb9ebde4","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_00c3e5c7a76728f526dce9a9787a6d842e1dfb6e5764bf29ee196fcf21ddb2f2","overall_assessment":"The primary policy concern is the violation of double-blind anonymity due to the explicit inclusion of author names, affiliations, and emails. Data usage is compliant with standard practices for public benchmarks. There are no ethical or plagiarism issues, but the paper lacks modern broader impact statements and code licensing details.","paper_id":"BJK3Xasel","paper_identity_sha256":"305843a37682a12f751687215e5e855ba8e81584952a8824b98621a75d8ac6ae","prompt_identity_sha256":"a94d40cabc7060d0552299f300ecf0ffde52be262a6f1b2fabb1252082f7727f","raw_response_sha256":"f974b16abf219d537b5e2e348d0a6ebec5bcb94f60f1137436c56d69fb90f5d0","request_identity_sha256":"30940dfa45ec77eda589869b3285066b3ba1b3eee162aa1c4db41c8261a8a3a5","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or responsible AI. Given that the work focuses on algorithmic efficiency and network architecture selection using standard public benchmarks (MNIST, Rectangles, Convex), there are no immediate ethical risks related to bias, harm to marginalized groups, or dual-use applications. The absence of an ethics statement is consistent with the scope of the technical contribution, which does not involve sensitive data or high-stakes decision-making contexts.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019"],"review_text":"The experiments utilize three standard benchmark datasets: MNIST, the rectangles images dataset, and the convex dataset (citing Bergstra & Bengio, 2012). These are widely used, public datasets that do not contain personally identifiable information (PII) or sensitive personal data. The paper does not explicitly state the licensing terms for these datasets, but their use in academic research is standard and generally compliant with open-data norms. No privacy violations or consent issues are apparent from the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (George Philipp, Jaime G. Carbonell), their institutional affiliation (Carnegie Mellon University), and their email addresses (georg@cmu.edu; jgc@cs.cmu.edu) on the title page. This violates the double-blind review policy typically enforced at venues like ICLR, as it directly reveals the identities of the authors and their affiliation. This is a significant anonymity violation.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper presents original contributions, including the nonparametric neural network framework, the CapNorm layer, and the AdaRad algorithm. The references section cites relevant prior work (e.g., Wei et al., 2016; Chen et al., 2016) appropriately, acknowledging the inspiration for the f-equivalence concept and network morphism. There is no evidence of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission within the visible text. The content appears to be original and properly attributed.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which are increasingly expected in modern ML submissions. However, the work is a fundamental algorithmic contribution to network architecture search, and its societal impact is indirect. The paper does not mention software or data licensing for the proposed method, nor does it provide code availability statements. While not a critical flaw for a 2017 submission, the lack of explicit broader impact discussion or code release information is a limitation in terms of reproducibility and transparency standards.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"ab2ebd536ec7604856c52b34f58d9210a4fc944d88e6ff3bebb5351e64538be6","paper_id":"BJK3Xasel","paper_ordinal":27,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"f974b16abf219d537b5e2e348d0a6ebec5bcb94f60f1137436c56d69fb90f5d0","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJK3Xasel","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"698f5ce6951eba9c891c77cf82746fb6f0382eb899144cfa6fe1c945fe8fb3ea","request_identity_sha256":"30940dfa45ec77eda589869b3285066b3ba1b3eee162aa1c4db41c8261a8a3a5","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":795,"prompt_tokens":17251,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18046},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"30940dfa45ec77eda589869b3285066b3ba1b3eee162aa1c4db41c8261a8a3a5","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}